    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40490" root="نكح" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ نُكَحَةٌ</span></b> , (S, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُكَحٌ</span></b>  (K) <i>A man
who marries much,</i> or <i>often:</i> (S, K, TA:) AZ
explains the former by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَدِيدُ النِّكَاحِ</span>, [app. meaning
<i>vehement in coitus,</i>] and mentions as its pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُكَحَاتٌ</span>:
(TA:) [and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَكَّاحٌ</span></b>  (A, TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تيس</span>, &amp;c.) signifies the same.]

